job_description:
# Head of Data and Insight
**Lead data, insight and responsible AI transformation at Demelza** At Demelza, we believe better insight leads to better decisions, stronger services and greater impact for children and families.
We are looking for an experienced and ambitious **Head of Data and Insight** to lead our organisation-wide Data and Insight function at an important point in its development.
This is an opportunity to shape how Demelza uses data, analytics, automation and responsible AI across the organisation. You will lead a multidisciplinary team, turn our Data and Governance Strategy into practical delivery and help colleagues to use trusted evidence to support informed decision~~s~~ -making and demonstrate impact.
You will have the professional autonomy to set direction, establish priorities and build a modern, resilient data function. Just as importantly, you will see the direct connection between your work and Demelza’s mission to provide extraordinary care and support to children and young people with serious or life-limiting conditions and their families.
**What you will do**Reporting to the Director of IT, Data and Governance, you will:
* lead the implementation and continued development of Demelza’s Data and Governance Strategy;
* provide visible leadership, coaching and direction to the Data and Insight team;
* strengthen data quality, ownership, governance and reporting confidence across the organisation;
* develop our business intelligence and analytics capability, turning complex data into clear, actionable insight;
* oversee the development of organisation MI, dashboards, reporting models and our data warehouse;
* establish transparent priorities for data, reporting, systems and improvement requests;
* identify opportunities to improve processes, reduce duplication and make better use of organisational capacity;
* lead the safe, ethical and proportionate adoption of AI and automation;
* oversee a portfolio of data applications, integrations and system improvements; and
* work alongside senior leaders, trustees and colleagues across Demelza to translate evidence into practical action and measurable benefits.
**About you**
You will be an experienced data, insight, analytics or applications leader who combines strategic thinking with practical delivery.
You will bring:
* experience of leading and developing an effective data, insight, reporting or information governance function;
* a strong track record of translating strategy into prioritised plans, measurable outcomes and sustainable improvements;
* experience of leading organisational change, digital transformation or complex delivery programmes;
* experience of business intelligence, reporting and visualisation, including Power BI or comparable technologies;
* a good understanding of data quality, data governance, information security and responsible data use;
* confidence identifying and implementing appropriate automation and AI-enabled opportunities within a well-governed environment;
* strong people leadership skills and the ability to build capability, resilience and shared accountability;
* the credibility to influence senior stakeholders and constructively challenge assumptions;
* the ability to communicate technical or complex information clearly to different audiences; and
* a curious, collaborative and solutions-focused approach.
You do not need to have worked in a hospice before. Experience in healthcare, charities or another regulated environment would be valuable, but we are equally interested in the transferable knowledge, leadership and perspective you could bring.
Most importantly, you will be motivated by the opportunity to use data and technology for a clear social purpose.
## Why join Demelza?
This is more than a data leadership role. It is an opportunity to:
* shape the future direction of data, insight, automation and AI at Demelza;
* influence strategic and operational decision-making across the organisation;
* build a clear, supportive and organisation-wide data service;
* lead transformational work with visible and measurable impact;
* develop a talented multidisciplinary team;
* work with colleagues who care deeply about the quality and impact of their work; and
* use your expertise to support extraordinary care for children and families.
For an informal chat, please call Claire Ellis-Waghorn, Director of IT, Data and Governance, on 01795 845261. Closing date - **Monday 2nd November 2026** Interview date - **Wednesday 11th November 2026** Demelza greatly values the benefits of a diverse team and embraces diversity, equality, and inclusion in all areas of its work. We are committed to building a diverse and authentic workplace, ensuring that our team reflects the diversity of the children and families we support. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds.
To find out how we process your personal data during the recruitment process, please refer to the Employee Recruitment Privacy Notice.
As part of our commitment to safer recruitment, all offers of employment are subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks, including a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check at a level relevant to the role.
Demelza is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of children, young people and vulnerable adults and expects all employees and volunteers to share this commitment.
Demelza is an equal opportunities employer. Registered Charity No. 1039651.
## About Demelza
Demelza delivers extraordinary care to extraordinary children who are facing serious or life-limiting conditions, throughout Kent, South East London and East Sussex. We’re here to support them and their families at every step – from first diagnosis and for as long as we’re needed. Demelza believes in care that doesn’t back down. Benefits include:
* Generous annual leave, with buy/sell opportunities and length of service awards
* Enhanced maternity pay for eligible employees
* Opportunity to remain in NHS Pension
* Cycle to work scheme
* Tech scheme
* Eye care vouchers
* Wellbeing events and support
* Access to benefits and wellbeing platform
* Access to training and development opportunities

# Forward Deployed Engineer
Remote
Remote
**Who We Are Seeking**
We are looking for a talented and dedicated engineer who thrives in fast-paced environments. In this role, you will lead product discovery with enterprise clients, unearthing real workflow friction and figuring out what actually needs to be built to turn pain points into business outcomes. You leverage modern AI-assisted coding tools, LLMs, and rapid prototyping workflows to iterate and ship at breakneck speed, turning discovery insights into live production code.
**Your Role and Responsibilities**
* Design, build, and maintain sophisticated AI agents and automated workflows for complex operational tasks.
* Deploy production-quality code and take ownership of solutions from product discovery through deployment and ongoing support;
* Leverage AI-coding tools to enhance code quality and test coverage
* Have significant influence over the technical and commercial direction of the product;
* Work directly with end-users to translate feedback into platform improvements;
* Partner with team to turn custom client builds into reusable platform features, tools, and documentation;
* Improve reliability through rigorous testing, monitoring, and iterative development;
* Independently diagnose and resolve complex technical issues in live customer environments;
* Stay at the forefront of AI automation and agentic systems.
**Essential Qualifications**
* 5+ years of professional experience in software engineering or a related technical role;
* Proven track record in a client-facing technical role such as Forward Deployed Engineer, Solutions Engineer, or Implementation Engineer;
* Strong proficiency in at least one modern programming language such as Python, TypeScript/JavaScript, Go, or Java;
* Deep expertise in AI/LLM prompting, structured output techniques, and agentic system design;
* Hands-on experience with RAG pipelines, evaluation, guardrails, and LLM observability;
* Experience building HR, ATS, CRM, or other enterprise systems;
* Practical understanding of enterprise security and compliance requirements, including SSO, GDPR, SOC 2, and OAuth;
* Experience working in an early-stage or high-growth technology company;
* Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment with changing requirements;
* Ability to troubleshoot complex technical problems independently;
* Strong communication skills and the ability to work directly with customers and technical stakeholders;
* Ability to work independently and as part of a team, managing multiple priorities in a dynamic environment;
* Advanced English, both spoken and written.
**Desirable Qualifications**
* Degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Software Engineering, or a related field;
* Familiarity with cloud environments (Azure, AWS, GCP) and backend infrastructure;
* Active use of AI development tools (ChatGPT, Claude, Copilot, Cursor, etc.);
* Equivalent practical experience and a strong portfolio of shipped AI products are equally valued;
* Experience working with international, cross-functional, and remote teams;
* Excellent written and oral communication skills.
**Who We Are** DevGrid is a top-tier software consulting company based in the UK, with a development hub in Brazil and operations spanning Europe and the US. We believe that world-class software can only be created by a motivated and enthusiastic team in an environment that fosters creativity and free thinking. Established in 2015, we aim to drive innovation and digital transformation by combining our robust business culture and exceptional engineers with forward-thinking business insights.
**What We Offer**
* Contract-based hiring
* Full-time opportunity (40 hours per week)
* 100% remote work/home office
* Performance-based bonuses tied to achievements and deliverables
* Open and flexible time-off policy
* Supportive and collaborative work environment
* Equipment program
* Paid days off per year + holidays (variable) + recess days
* Sponsorship program for relevant courses and training
**For more information, visit:**
Website: https://devgrid.co.uk/
Glassdoor: https://www.glassdoor.com.br/Vis%C3%A3o-geral/Trabalhar-na-DevGrid-EI\_IE2920141.13,20.htm
\*\*All DevGrid positions are open to individuals from all backgrounds (including all races, colors, nationalities, religions, genders, sexual orientations, disabilities, ages, or other applicable characteristics), promoting equal opportunities and affirmative action.
If you're interested in the job opening and our mission, come join us on this journey!

# Principal Geospatial Developer
#### Submission deadline: 9th October 2026
## About Prior + Partners
Prior + Partners is a specialist placemaking practice integrating masterplanning, planning and economics to unlock the potential of places and communities.
Our work spans district, city and regional scales, moving between strategic visioning, concept and detailed masterplans, planning and implementation. We work on major regeneration projects, new communities, mixed-use districts and strategic development frameworks in the UK and internationally.
We are now seeking an experienced and technically strong **Principal Geospatial Developer** to join our Digital Innovation team in London and help deliver our growing portfolio of digital and data-led work.
Please download the full job specification here.
## About the role
The successful candidate will be an experienced geospatial professional who combines spatial analysis and data science with building the tools and methods that deliver it, and who has experience working in the built environment.
You will be responsible for the technical oversight across all digital innovation work, responsible for delivering our work across client projects and products. This spans hands-on consultancy and delivery for clients in the built environment, through to building our own products, including Place+, our digital placemaking platform.
You will work closely with our Head of Digital Innovation and Associate Director Applied Innovation on technical direction, and you will own the delivery of it. This is a senior, hands-on role. The final job title and level will be agreed based on the candidate’s experience and capability.
## Key Responsibilities
The role will include:
* Delivering the technical side of client consultancy projects across spatial analytics, planning and the built environment, end to end;
* Translating built-environment problems into analytical approaches and technical solutions;
* Carrying out spatial and data analysis, including statistical and machine learning methods, to answer client and planning questions;
* Developing and refining analytical methods and models that can be reused across projects;
* Owning the architecture and build of spatial data pipelines at scale, including PostGIS, vector tiles and tile servers;
* Building and shipping client-facing tools, dashboards and web maps, including the development of Place+ and its product lines;
* Communicating findings clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders;
* Setting the technical standard for the team, mentoring others and line managing where needed;
* Supporting business development by scoping work, shaping bids and representing our technical capability to clients and stakeholders.
## The candidate we are looking for will have
* Strong geospatial skills, including PostGIS, spatial analysis at scale, vector tiles and GIS platforms such as ArcGIS or QGIS;
* Strong data science skills, including Python, SQL, statistics and machine learning applied to spatial problems;
* Experience of modern frontend and web mapping development, including HTML, JavaScript and with a focus on geospatial libraries;
* Experience in the built environment, including planning, spatial analytics, infrastructure or a closely related sector, and the ability to talk credibly to the people in it;
* A track record of delivering technical consultancy projects end to end and shipping polished products;
* Commercial awareness and confidence working with clients, shaping scopes and supporting bids;
* A self-directed and pragmatic approach, with the judgement to know which technical calls matter;
* Design sensibility for product and data visualisation would be beneficial, but is not essential;
* Experience building AI into analytical products would be beneficial, but is not essential.
## How to apply
Job title and salary will be commensurate with experience. We offer the opportunity to further your career within a busy, growing and multidisciplinary practice, working alongside urban designers, planners, economists, spatial data specialists and public realm professionals.
To apply, please submit your CV in confidence to: careers@priorpartners.com
Prior + Partners is an Employee-Owned Trust and an equal opportunities employer committed to creating an open, respectful environment where people can build lasting careers and do their best work. We welcome applications from candidates returning to the profession following a career break.

Deskside Technician
Job ID#:
45525
Category:
DWS-Local Operations
Location:
London, United Kingdom
Position Type:
Employee
Job Description
**This is a 4 months fixed term contract**
Working in a fast paced, constantly evolving environment, you will be responsible for providing a high level of customer service and hands-on support. This is a fantastic opportunity to join an ambitious company operating at the forefront of their industry, and play a key role in ensuring the successful delivery of a premium IT support service.
**Job responsibilities**
* Provide face-to-face IT support for users, ensuring timely and effective resolution of issues;
* Manage support queues using ServiceNow, maintaining efficient ticket handling and prioritization;
* Demonstrate the ability to multi-task, adhere to processes and procedures, and follow pre-established guidelines;
* Coordinate with third-party vendors to resolve hardware and software issues as required;
* Perform hardware installation, relocation, and de-installation tasks;
* Diagnose and resolve issues related to personal hardware, including PCs, laptops, printers, and scanners;
* Maintain, analyze, and troubleshoot end-user computing problems, both hardware and software-related;
* Test system and application changes and prepare scripts in MS Windows 11 and MS Office 365 environments;
* Conduct basic Microsoft 365 administration, including Entra ID and Intune management.
* Install and configure equipment, cables, outlets, and other hardware required for IMAC implementations;
* Manage Windows 11 software, patches, and updates using Intune and Autopilot;
* Provide support for AV rooms and conferences, utilizing software such as MS Teams and Zoom;
* Offer remote and onsite support to users in other locations within the country as needed.
* Troubleshoot and resolve issues with warehouse equipment, such as label printers and handheld scanners;
* Handle user onboarding and offboarding processes efficiently;
* Maintain and manage mobile devices using MDM via Intune;
* Lead asset refresh campaigns within the country, ensuring smooth execution;
* Keep CMDB records updated using ServiceNow;
* Coordinate and manage local IT projects as required.
Job Requirements
**Requirement's**
* A minimum of 5 years of experience in an IT support role;
* Proficiency in Windows 10/11 and MS Office 365 environments;
* Strong diagnostic skills for hardware issues, including PCs, laptops, and printers;
* ITIL certification is an advantage;
* Familiarity with ServiceNow is highly desirable;
* Knowledge of remote administrative tools in Windows 10/11 environments;
* Understanding of LAN, wireless, and VPN technologies for basic troubleshooting;
* Experience with Intune and Autopilot for device management;
* Working knowledge of Active Directory and MS Azure;
* Familiarity with network-connected printers and multifunctional devices;
* A willingness to learn and adapt to new technologies;
* Positive and proactive attitude with strong teamwork capabilities;
* Excellent communication skills and a focus on service delivery;
* Ability to manage stress and handle workloads effectively;
* Experience with Zebra devices is considered an advantage;
* Fluency in English is required.
The preceding job description had been designed to indicate the general nature and level of work performed by employees within this classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties and responsibilities required of employees assigned to this job.
**What****we offer**
* Competitive salary and benefits package;
* AFB bonus;
* Private health scheme including Private Medical, Dental, Optical and Holiday Travel;
* Extra vacation days;
* Opportunities to learn and develop: training programs;
* Personalized career path within the organization;
* Exposure to an international environment as part of a multicultural team spread across Europe.
**Work conditions**
* Working hours: 40 working hours per week
* Contract type: 4 months fixed term
* Working setup (hybrid, on site, remote): 100% onsite
**What's next**
It's best to apply today, because job postings can be taken down and we wouldn't want you to miss this opportunity. In case you need further information, just send us a message at recruitmentEMEA@stefanini.com and we'll be happy to assist!
